cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the manuscript below."
title: "Dissecting Serial Sparse Activation: On the Necessity of Chain Depth and What Memory and Routing Each Carry"
abstract: >-
  Code and measurement logs for a controlled deconstruction of serially chained,
  hard-routed sparse activation: which part of the chain carries the sentence-level
  metric, what routing contributes once the content correspondence is broken, and
  how the ordering between sparse and dense architectures depends on the metric
  and on the device.
